WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.003
Every June, the wind over India turns

2
00:00:02.003 --> 00:00:02.804
around.

3
00:00:02.804 --> 00:00:04.962
And a whole country waits for it.

4
00:00:05.362 --> 00:00:07.138
Through spring, the land heats up much

5
00:00:07.138 --> 00:00:08.845
faster than the sea.

6
00:00:08.845 --> 00:00:10.354
Hot air over the land rises,

7
00:00:10.354 --> 00:00:12.117
and the pressure there falls.

8
00:00:12.517 --> 00:00:14.258
So cooler, wet air from the ocean

9
00:00:14.258 --> 00:00:16.116
is pulled in towards the land.

10
00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:18.576
That inflow is the south-west monsoon.

11
00:00:18.975 --> 00:00:21.111
It usually reaches Kerala around the first

12
00:00:21.111 --> 00:00:23.224
of June, and covers the whole country

13
00:00:23.224 --> 00:00:25.126
by about the eighth of July.

14
00:00:25.527 --> 00:00:27.466
When these winds meet the Western Ghats,

15
00:00:27.466 --> 00:00:28.464
they rise, cool,

16
00:00:28.464 --> 00:00:30.937
and pour rain on the sea-facing side.

17
00:00:30.937 --> 00:00:33.317
The far side stays much drier.

18
00:00:33.317 --> 00:00:34.836
That is a rain shadow.

19
00:00:35.236 --> 00:00:36.501
From June to September,

20
00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:38.754
India gets about three-quarters of its rain

21
00:00:38.754 --> 00:00:40.087
for the whole year.

22
00:00:40.487 --> 00:00:41.764
For your answer:

23
00:00:41.764 --> 00:00:42.879
the land heats,

24
00:00:42.879 --> 00:00:45.851
pressure falls, sea winds rush in,

25
00:00:45.851 --> 00:00:47.892
and the hills wring out the rain.

